liz: Support repro: during an embeddings migration repeated 429s + context trimming produced garbled outputs. our error-ref mentions fallbacks but has no runnable snippet. can someone add a tiny JS + Python pattern and a 5-bullet runbook we can paste?

omar: I can do JS. keep it minimal: catch 429, emit metric, trim context, downgrade model, retry once with backoff.

rachel: Call out when NOT to auto-downgrade (legal/safety) and recommend single retry. also include Console event name `client.retry` with tags `retry_reason` and `fallback_model`.

omar: JS draft (compact):
```js
try {
  await client.generate({model: 'redwood-large-v1', prompt: bigPrompt, max_tokens: 1024})
} catch (e) {
  if (e instanceof RateLimitError) {
    client.metrics.increment('client.retry', {retry_reason: 'context_trim'})
    await client.generate({model: 'redwood-small-v1', prompt: trimContext(bigPrompt, 2048), max_tokens: 256})
  }
}
```

liz: Nice. I'll add a 1-paragraph tradeoffs note (quality vs cost/latency) and the 5 bullet runbook: reproduce minimal case; confirm 429s (not infra); try local trim; add fallback snippet; monitor Console fallback_rate.

